# Commit Message Style

Use conventional commit format for every commit in this repo.

- Subject line format: `<type>(<scope>): <summary>`
- Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `chore`, `test`
- Keep summary concise, present tense, and under ~72 chars when possible.
- Scope should reflect the touched area (for example: `prototype`, `deploy`, `auth`, `ui`, `docs`).
- Add a short body only when needed, focused on **why** (not just file lists).

## Examples

```text
feat(prototype): add role-based route guard for lead pages
fix(deploy): clear stale Next.js cache handling on startup
docs(plan): add follow-up TODO notes for staffing workflows
chore(git): standardize commit and push workflow
```
